name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q13_2025'

question 'Which of the following is an example of an "edge case" for a search bar?'

wrong 'A user typing the exact name of a product that exists.'
wrong 'A user typing a very common word like "the".'
right 'A user leaving the search bar empty and clicking "Submit."'
wrong 'A user clicking a link to the "Home" page.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 9

Edge cases are inputs that occur at the "edges" of expected use, such as empty strings, very long strings, or special symbols that might cause a function to fail if not handled properly.
MARKDOWN
